  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 134 PM CDT Sun Jul 26 2026\n\nSummer-time heat continues. Heat remains the main concern through \nnext week with a moderate to major risk of heat related impacts \nacross S TX, and an increasing risk to extreme impacts at times \nacross the Brush Country. However, conditions will be drier across \nthe western areas, thus heat indices will generally range from 105-\n109. Heat advisories may be needed at times during the upcoming week \nwith heat indices of 110-114 across mainly the Coastal Bend and \nVictoria Crossroads where the afternoon humidity will be highest. \n\nThe mid/upper level high pressure system leading to the increased \nheat risks will also lead to very low to nil rain chances. Models do \nindicate a couple of weak inverted troughs/easterly waves through \nthe period, thus can not rule out a few weak showers, mainly morning \nstreamer showers along the coast and along the afternoon sea breeze. \nRain chances are generally 0-15% through the period.",
